AI Engineer / Business AI Integration Specialist
About the company:
Paynet
specializes in B2B and B2C technology projects in the financial services (Fintech) sector, such as electronic payment processing, customer loyalty management systems, e-money services, and online payment acceptance solutions.
Our core values are innovation, quality, and customer satisfaction. We strive to deliver the best solutions and services, continuously seek new growth opportunities, and stay up to date with the latest trends and technologies in the industry.
Responsibilities:
Designing and implementing AI-based solutions for internal business process optimization;
Collaborating with business and IT teams to identify opportunities for automation and integration of AI tools;
Developing and maintaining AI agents using Python, FastAPI, and LLM APIs (e.g., OpenAI);
Automating routine, logic-driven workflows across departments;
Contributing to prompt engineering, metadata modeling, and knowledge extraction;
Supporting backend integrations using PostgreSQL, Redis, and REST APIs;
Participating in the development of workflows simulating decision-making processes;
Delivering training sessions and creating documentation to promote AI adoption within teams;
Maintaining clean, well-documented code and participating in regular code reviews;
Keeping up with the latest developments in AI, automation, and autonomous agent frameworks.
Requirements:
Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field;
Basic programming skills in Python or other scripting languages;
Understanding of web technologies and RESTful APIs;
Interest in AI, NLP, and automation (experience with LLMs is a plus);
Familiarity with databases (SQL/NoSQL) and version control systems like Git;
Strong analytical thinking, attention to detail, and a proactive attitude;
Good communication and documentation skills;
Ability to work in a team environment and adapt to changing priorities.
We offer:
Participation in exciting and large-scale projects;
Challenging and engaging tasks that help develop your skills;
Competitive salary, reviewed annually, along with a full social package;
Comfortable work environment with an excellent work-life balance;
Stable work schedule (Monday - Friday, 09:00–18:00), with a one-hour lunch break;
Free English language courses;
Opportunities for personal and professional development, including additional courses;
Team-building activities, corporate gifts, and bonuses for special occasions (e.g., birthday, childbirth);
Cozy office located near Valea Trandafirilor Park, at Decebal 6 (Botanica);
Coffee and snacks at the office to keep you energized and in a good mood.
To apply for this job, candidates should send their CV to
hr.office@paynet.md
with subject line: „AI Integration Specialist”.
Selected candidates will be invited for an interview.

